  "question": {
    "text": "Two blocks&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> of equal mass are released on two sides of a fixed wedge&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> as shown in the figure. Find the acceleration of the centre of mass of blocks&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>. Neglect friction.<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0073_985ba8b7eb8c.jpg\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 139px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, downwards",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi></math>, downwards",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, upwards",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>3</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mi>g</mi> <mtext>,</mtext> </mrow> </math> downwards",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Acceleration of both the blocks will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;or <math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mi>g</mi> </mrow> <mrow> <msqrt> <mn>2</mn> </msqrt> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;at right angles to each other. Now,<br /><br /><b><u><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0073_be8cc42ec605.jpg\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 161px;\" /></u></b><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mtext>a</mtext><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mtext>com</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>A</mtext></msub><msub><mover><mtext>a</mtext><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mtext>A</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>B</mtext></msub><msub><mover><mtext>a</mtext><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mtext>B</mtext></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>A</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>B</mtext></msub></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />Here,&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>com</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mtext>A</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mtext>B</mtext></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>g</mi></math>&nbsp; &nbsp;(downwards)</p>"
  }
